# Moderate prompt/output size, high concurrency - deliberately pushes the
# engine past its max-num-seqs so requests queue. Use this to drive the
# vllm-cache-queue-pressure dashboard (waiting requests, KV cache
# utilisation, inter-token latency stalls).
#
# Token counts are intentionally short and fixed (not meant to mimic a real
# workload) - concurrency, not prompt realism, is the variable under test
# here. This matches how NVIDIA GenAI-Perf and vLLM's own stress configs
# approach throughput testing: short, low-variance token counts so the only
# thing driving queueing/saturation is concurrency.
BENCH_TARGET=http://change-me.change-me-namespace.svc.cluster.local:8000
BENCH_MODEL=change-me
BENCH_TOKENIZER=change-me
BENCH_PROMPT_TOKENS=256
BENCH_OUTPUT_TOKENS=128
BENCH_CONCURRENCY=64
BENCH_MAX_REQUESTS=1000
BENCH_MAX_DURATION_SECONDS=180
BENCH_VERIFY_TLS=true
